# Fields Demo (watext / watranslate)
writeassist_fields_demo_title = AI field widgets for plain form fields
writeassist_fields_demo_intro = Textareas and inputs without a WYSIWYG editor can get an AI button just by adding a CSS class - no extra JavaScript needed, WriteAssist detects the fields automatically (including ones added later via MBlock etc.).
writeassist_fields_demo_watext_hint = Adds a magic-wand button: generate, rewrite, summarize, expand or edit via a custom prompt.
writeassist_fields_demo_watranslate_hint = Adds a translate button that translates the field content directly into the chosen language.
writeassist_fields_demo_input_label = Input field
writeassist_fields_demo_input_placeholder = e.g. headline or meta title...
writeassist_fields_demo_textarea_label = Textarea
writeassist_fields_demo_textarea_placeholder = Try it here...
writeassist_fields_demo_translate_sample = Hello, how are you?
writeassist_fields_demo_watext_provider = Current AI provider: {0}. Change it under
writeassist_fields_demo_watranslate_provider = Current translation engine: {0}. Change it under
writeassist_fields_demo_usage_title = Usage in your own code
writeassist_fields_demo_usage_intro = Just add the class to the form field - works in modules, YForm forms, MForm and any backend page:
writeassist_fields_demo_usage_note = Both classes can be combined (the field then gets both buttons).
writeassist_fields_demo_combined_hint = Both classes at once - the field gets two buttons side by side (generate and translate).
writeassist_fields_demo_maxlength_hint = An existing maxlength attribute is respected: the result is automatically truncated if needed, with a visible notice instead of silent data loss.

